3.1. Estimation of parameters specific to the model
The value of the shape coefficient, δM, calculated from the allometric relationship between length and flesh volume (Fig. 3) was 0.64 for a P. margaritifera larva (n = 24). At the D-stage, therefore, which corresponds to the very first stage of larval development, the flesh mass was 134 ng for a length of 80 μm. This mass increased progressively to reach close to 2100 ng for a length of 200 μm in the first pediveligerian larvae.
