The forcing data (Chl a and temperature) are presented in Fig. 8. The concentrations of Chl a varied between 0.23 and 0.62 μg Chl a l-1 with daily values between 0.04 and 1.4 μg Chl a l-1. Variation along the bathymetric gradient appeared to be greater than variations at the scale of the lagoon. An increasing concentration gradient was observed between the surface and bottom. The strongest concentrations were measured in the west of the lagoon at station 01 and in the extreme east. The central part of the lagoon appeared poorer, notably near the pass (stations 03 and 04). Mean temperaturesvaried between 29.2 and 29.4 °C. Although relatively weak, temperature variation appeared greater between the different areas of the lagoon than according to depth, the water column being relatively homogeneous.
